// One of the seven contract pins for THE BOTTOM-PRODUCTION RULE (the
// sep04a audit, 2026-09-06): a fused bottom's STALE bit follows its
// trigger, exactly like a value's. Each pin drives a STANDING bottom
// through one placeholder-consuming emitter path under a `<-` target
// — the sep04a observable, since a `<-` target's binding re-publishes
// whenever its initializer PRODUCES, so a bottom re-minted FRESH lands
// in the write's own cycle and eats it. Interp: the write survives.
//
// Path: a consulted guard that bottoms — the UNDETERMINED return
// (flow.rs, emit_select_node_tail's undetermined arm)
//
// Every one of these was already correct when the audit ran — the
// fold was present at each of these call sites, and only the
// tail-position select (pins 00/02) had lost it. They are pins
// because the fold is now the placeholder's own job
// (`emit_bottom_placeholder(cx, typ, fires)`), and a refactor that
// hands the raw pair back to a consumer re-opens the class. Each was
// confirmed RED against a build with every placeholder STALE fold
// removed, so this green is evidence and not absence.
{
    let g = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {
        m if (m / 0) > 0 => m,
        m => m + 1
    };
    let v = g(1);
    v <- 1;
    v
}
